sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 13.39 µm in Danio margaritatus (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 75.3/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1. Linear lambda_c is 13.39 µm by construction and the 1D PDE growth-rate series matches the eigenvalue (Pearson r = 0.99999995, RMSE = 5.5e-4 /s). Danio albolineatus is stable at this rung (sigma_max = -0.080 /s). Danio nigrofasciatus selects 17.80 µm. The adult photograph's pearl nearest-neighbour gap is 510 µm, so the elementary mode is not resolved. First-pass gaps: the diffusion-ratio sweep had to be checked at the anchor, the pearl hull had to be kept on the blue flank, circularity had to be a polygon quotient rather than a clipped raster, and the comparison figure had to separate the nonlinear FFT peak (17.22 µm) from the linear law. Overall 75.3/100 (faithfulness 72.6, reproducibility 81.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 23fb4b106f961ebb8b80abe7209257c902f834ad; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 76, Morphological realism / specimen match 72, Parameter expressivity 74, Morphometric validation 68, Source and data traceability 86, Code-to-model traceability 76, Reproducibility package 82. Output judged: docs/media/danio_margaritatus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 23fb4b106f961ebb8b80abe7209257c902f834ad, image/png, 630986 B, 1512×984 px, artifact_sha256 8eac595b6d5b6eb28291aff92e3ce8801578927e4be889341429924640adbc4e (sha256 8eac595b6d5b6eb28291aff92e3ce8801578927e4be889341429924640adbc4e), spec_fingerprint b77145afbb1daaa36679993eab12015d9069adc4fe8d9a9b382f23a8172ce984. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: b77145afbb1daaa36679993eab12015d9069adc4fe8d9a9b382f23a8172ce984; artifact_sha256: 8eac595b6d5b6eb28291aff92e3ce8801578927e4be889341429924640adbc4e; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/danio_margaritatus_turing_wavelength_s0/danio_margaritatus_specimen.jpg=48a9005afc001e30..., datasets/danio_margaritatus_turing_wavelength_s0/danio_margaritatus_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=ecf0d9be62697438...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: a reaction-diffusion system can be stable at k = 0 and unstable at a finite k_c. | Nakamasu et al. 2009: melanophore-xanthophore interactions have the short-range activation and long-range inhibition structure of a Turing system. | Quigley et al. 2004 and Patterson et al. 2014: Danio species differ in how stripes and spots are deployed. | Conway, Chen & Mayden 2008: the celestial pearl danio is a miniature Danio.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg parameters that set lambda_c to 1.339e-05 m for margaritatus, stability for albolineatus, and 17.80 µm for nigrofasciatus. | 0.018 m catalog length applied to the pearl-field major axis.; transfer_boundary: The adult photograph samples at about 21 µm per pixel, so 13.39 µm is not a direct measurement on that image. | Predecessor and successor parameters are not fits to photographs of those species.; does_not_claim: That adult pearl spacing equals 13.39 µm. | That the convex-hull animation is a copy of the photograph.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Keep the pearl hull on the blue flank (drop wood and plants) and report polygon circularity instead of a raster quotient clipped at 1.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Diffusion-ratio sweep at fixed D_u must decrease lambda_c and equal 13.39 µm at delta = 40.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Print the bootstrap 95% CI and the nonlinear FFT peak on the comparison figure, separate from the linear 13.39 µm law.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Replace the axis-aligned ellipse occupancy model with the flank principal-axis chord model and report the odd-bin Pearson without forcing it above 0.98.'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.753"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single agent; no second provider)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

